  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "Groups, studies and trials that exist",
   "text": "The Canadian Society for Mucopolysaccharide & Related Diseases Inc, a patient group in Canada, says it supports families affected by MPS IIID [E9ef6d0f]. AIMPS ETS, a patient group in Italy, says it was created to support children and adults with these rare metabolic diseases [Ea6b3adc]. The Cure Sanfilippo Foundation in the United States says its mission is to fund research toward a cure or treatment for children with Sanfilippo Syndrome [E6c5b837]. Fundación Stop Sanfilippo in Spain says it researches to find a treatment for Sanfilippo syndrome [E70e86a1]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a newborn screening study called Early Check is active for MPS IIID in the United States [Ef817ec9]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a completed natural history study looked at Sanfilippo Syndrome Type D in the United States [E2fea033]. According to NIH RePORTER, a grant titled 'Evaluation of Clinical Outcome Assessment (COA) and Potential Biomarkers to Facilitate Interventional Trial for Mucopolysaccharidosis IIID Patients' studies MPS IIID [Ec1eec8d]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a gene transfer trial for MPS IIIA, a related disease, is recruiting in Australia, Spain and the United States and tests an intervention called UX111 [Eebc4df2, E3023148].",
